   "text": {
    "L1": "To compare fractions, first check that the wholes are the same size.",
    "L2": "Here is a common mistake: thinking 1/8 is bigger than 1/4 because 8 is bigger than 4.",
    "L3": "That is not true. Cutting one whole into more equal parts makes each part smaller, so 1/8 is less than 1/4.",
    "L4": "Now compare 2/5 and 2/3. Both fractions have two pieces.",
    "L5": "A third is bigger than a fifth because the same whole is cut into fewer equal parts.",
    "L6": "So two bigger pieces beat two smaller pieces: 2/3 is greater than 2/5.",
    "L7": "When the bottom numbers match, more pieces means more, like 5/7 and 3/7. When the top numbers match, bigger pieces win.",
    "L8": "Your turn: choose the fraction that is greater than 2/5."
   },
